	"notes": "This is about as simple as a blog can get: one column of text, centred on the page, nothing else. On a phone that column just fills the screen with a little padding on each side. Past about 672 pixels wide the column stops growing and locks to exactly 632 pixels — the scan shows that same number on a laptop screen and on an ultrawide monitor, so a bigger screen only adds quiet space on both sides, never a longer line of text. There is no menu, no sidebar and no images in the list, so nearly all of the page's personality comes from the pink headline colour rather than from the layout.",
